  "assessment": [
    "All 16 synthetic runs pass both security and strict 2,000ms functional gate, with 200 normally masked events per trial and zero fail-closed events.",
    "Four platform callers show highest observed median normally masked throughput (10.074/s); virtual at four show 9.606/s.",
    "Eight callers remain functionally eligible in this brief workload but median throughput drops to about 8.2/s and p95 grows to about 1.15-1.17s.",
    "Platform and virtual median comparisons are mixed across 1/2/4/8; do not claim a causal advantage from two trials per group.",
    "All runs have the same native ONNX workload (220 calls, 890 windows) and preserve numeric per-instance ordering despite physical write inversions.",
    "Post-shutdown memory snapshots show model resources being released, not a native peak or long soak guarantee.",
    "Previous one-shot 10-caller runs failed functionality. The transition from repeatable 8-caller success to 10-caller failure warrants targeted 8/9/10/12 re-testing and longer steady-state tests.",
    "Waves of synchronous callers do not model asynchronous/real-world arrival rates, cross-JVM total order, or sustained overload."
  ],
  "provisional_action": "Use 4 platform callers for the next reference performance and correctness run. Treat 8 as a demonstrated brief functional candidate, not validated production limit. Next test 8,9,10,12 with repeated AB/BA modes; keep existing worker, queue and deadline unchanged.",
  "evidence_limits": "Synthetic known fixtures, only two repetitions per setting, no sustained soak or telemetry for in-flight working-set peaks. Zero failures observed is not proof of zero failure probability."
}
